  "sources": [
    "style-research ch.2 §10 Afrobeats / dancehall-influenced mainstream",
    "style-research ch.1 Cross-genre engine constants (MPC swing scale)",
    "Wikipedia — One drop rhythm (the kick moves to beat 3 and beat 1 is left empty)",
    "Wikipedia — Steppers (reggae/dancehall drum pattern with the kick on all four beats)"
  ],
  "notes": "The one drop is an absence: nothing on beat 1, the kick landing on 3 underneath the rim, so every bar hangs for half its length before it drops. Hats swing springy at 57% with the open hat on the &s, rim and perc answer between the beats, and the bass fills the hole the missing downbeat leaves. Two- to four-chord minor vamps, sevenths where the record wants warmth, major brightness when it turns celebratory. Confidence is medium: the compendium's dancehall-pop entry fixes the tempo, the vamp length and the clave-locked melodic cell, but the one-drop/steppers kick grammar comes from the general reggae drum-pattern references rather than from a section of its own. ⚠ **`drums.kick.lockTo808` removed (2026-08-17, 808 gate).** This kit has no 808 — `bass808` is `null` here or in the parent it inherits — and `lockTo808` is the one parameter that says *how much of the kick the 808 follows*, so in this file it described a pairing that does not exist: `generators::drums::bass808` returns on `block.is_none()` before the value is ever read, which makes it provably dead here. Where it was NOT dead was in the artists and producers who extend this kit and author an 808 of their own: they inherited the zero, `kicks.iter().filter(|_| rng.random_bool(0.0))` kept nothing, and their sub lane was silent at every seed — `bass808::every_shipped_model_with_an_808_produces_a_playable_line` reported \"no 808 at all\" for 35 of them. Removing it restores the engine's documented default of 1.0 for exactly those children and changes nothing here. ⚠ No researched claim moved: this kit's own statement about the 808 is the `bass808: null` beside it, and that is untouched.",
